2017-11-03 16:35 GMT+01:00 Tom Snijders <tom.snijders at nuffield.ox.ac.uk<mailto:tom.snijders at nuffield.ox.ac.uk>>:
Dear Filippo,

The error probably has to do with multi-threading, I guess you have useCluster=TRUE. Try to use a single process first, with useCluster=FALSE.
Another advice for error interpretation is to request
traceback()
which will give you information about where the error occurred.

A general advice about asking advice for errors is to tell us not only the error but also about what you did to produce the error.

Cheers,
Tom


